{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Iron and copper are your lock.</b> Now he speaks against all Israel — that their mighty men would sit in the frontier cities and lock it so that the enemies could not enter it, as though it were closed with locks and bolts of iron and copper. Another interpretation: <b>Iron and copper are your lock</b> — your land is locked by mountains from which iron and copper are hewn, and the land of Asher was the lock of the land of Israel (Sifrei)." "<b>And as your days, so your wealth.</b> And as the days that are good for you — which are the days of your beginning, the days of your youth — so shall the days of your old age be, which are longing, flowing, and wasting away. Another interpretation: <b>And as your days, so your wealth</b> — according to the count of your days: all the days that you do the will of the Omnipresent — your wealth shall be, that all the lands shall flow silver and gold to the land of Israel, that it be blessed with fruits and all the lands are sustained from it and draw their silver and gold to it; אשקו״רנט — the silver and gold perishes from them, for they pour it out to your land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "The la'az אשקו״רנט is Old French escorant or equivalent, meaning 'flowing/running away, perishing'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:56.307261896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}